  "id": "COMPOUND:34512 - PROTEIN:710",
  "verbalization": "Conferol is implicated in the target pathway leading to ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Conferol acts as a target for multiple compounds, including Sophoraflavanone A, 6-Ethyl-4-hydroxy-5-methyl-3-[[2,4,6-trihydroxy-3-(3-methyl-2-butenyl)-5-(2-methyl-1-oxopropyl)phenyl]methyl]-2 h-pyran-2-one, and Cis-Bis(Methylthio)Silvatin. These compounds are all known to interact with the ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1, indicating a potential mechanism where Conferol serves as a mediator in the signaling or metabolic pathway that ultimately targets this protein. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Conferol in facilitating the interaction between these compounds and the ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1, suggesting a broader functional relationship that may involve the regulation of cellular processes through the modulation of this protein.",
